+**Expression-only prose is Auto-applicable**, tool-grounded either by a rule a
+prose guard the project ships reports (doctrine-index, link,
+instruction-budget, markdown-lint, gloss, pin, comment-block) or by a recorded
+**preservation check** — the passage's normative statements listed before and
+after, shown identical — as Validation Rigor's non-testable substitute. The
+audit row names the grounding used.
+
+**External contract**, for prose, is a normative rule a reader outside the PR
+relies on. Wording changing no such rule is not an external-contract change: it
+neither trips the Auto-applicable disqualifier nor routes to Needs sign-off on
+the external-interface clause alone.
+
+**A file the PR itself introduces** — a documentation, doctrine, or skill file
+absent from the PR's base under git rename detection, and a new code file's
+comments — carries no external contract until merge: review-loop edits to that
+prose are internal, applied and batched into the iteration's action commit,
+reviewed as new content in the diff. A moved or renamed file is pre-existing;
+new code keeps its ordinary routes.
+
 **Meaning-class prose on a surface that predates the PR keeps the
 Needs-sign-off route**, and on a signed spec bundle is refused to a
 `/spec-kickoff` delta re-walkthrough per the meta-spec's writer obligations.
